\import{base-macros}
\author{kellenkanarios}
\title{Commit is a state transition, not an allocation}
\taxon{Card}
\tag{card}
\meta{anki}{1786316439336}

\prompt{A store's lifetime: when is its [[UNB6]] slot allocated, and what changes at [[BI4H]] commit?}{
  The slot is allocated at \strong{dispatch/rename}, not at commit. It has to exist before the store executes: that is where the address and data get written in, and where younger loads find the value to [[GXCN]].

  Commit is only a \strong{state transition}. The entry stops being speculative — it becomes a \em{senior store}, and is now eligible to drain. Nothing reaches the cache at that instant.
}
